sub:assertion {
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/approach/trabecular-stress-alignment-wolffs-law--gemini-4-argon--3> a prov:Plan, delphi:TestableHypothesis ;
    rdfs:label "Single-trabecula shear-resorption test on longitudinal in vivo micro-CT scans" ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/problem/trabecular-stress-alignment-wolffs-law> ;
    dct:description "Test the causal core of `thompson1917-ch16-06` and `thompson1917-ch16-07` directly at the single-strut level by registering baseline (t_0) and follow-up (t_1) 3D micro-CT volumes from altered-loading or malunited-fracture cohorts. For each individual trabecular strut segmented at t_0, compute its axial unit tangent vector n_strut and solve the whole-bone micro-FE problem under the experimental load vector to obtain the local resolved shear stress tau_s = ||sigma . n_strut - (n_strut . sigma . n_strut) n_strut|| and normal axial strain energy density U_n.\n\nOverlay the registered t_1 scan to classify every surface voxel into formation, quiescence, or resorption (Christen et al. 2014). Fit a pre-registered logistic mixed-effects model testing whether oblique struts with high shear-to-normal ratio tau_s / |sigma_n| experience selective osteoclastic resorption on their shear-loaded flanks and apposition rotating n_strut toward the nearest principal stress eigenvector e_1(sigma), compared against a scalar strain-energy remodeling model that ignores stress obliquity." ;

    delphi:proposedTest "The directional shear-to-normal stress ratio tau_s / |sigma_n| predicts strut resorption and angular rotation Delta_theta toward e_1(sigma) with AUROC >= 0.65 and beats the scalar strain-energy model by Delta_BIC > 10." ;
    delphi:context "Fails if: Remodeling probability depends only on scalar strain magnitude (or proximity to marrow surfaces) with no statistically significant partial effect of strut-to-principal-stress obliquity angle." ;
    delphi:hypothesisType "approach/data-test" ;
    skos:note "Steps: 1. Locate and retrieve paired time-lapse in vivo micro-CT volumes (baseline and post-loading follow-up) of loaded trabecular bone from public repositories or author depositions. 2. Perform rigid and bone-boundary landmark registration between t_0 and t_1 scans to map surface formation and resorption sites at voxel resolution. 3. Decompose the micro-FE stress tensor on each t_0 strut into axial normal stress sigma_n and transverse shear stress tau_s. 4. Compare predictive log-likelihood (AUROC) of the directional shear-removal model (`thompson1917-ch16-06`) against the isotropic scalar strain-energy density model." ;
    skos:note "Difficulty (proposer's estimate of completion within about a month of agent time): long-shot" ;
    skos:note "Missing: Raw registered time-lapse in vivo micro-CT voxel pairs from load-redirection experiments (such as the sheep calcaneus or bird knee cohorts) are not openly deposited in public repositories, and the swarm has no animal facility or micro-CT scanner to generate them." ;
    skos:note "Tool: micro-ct-morphometry" ;
    skos:note "Tool: finite-element-analysis" ;
    skos:note "Tool: data-test" ;
    skos:related <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/thompson1917-ch16-05> ;
    skos:related <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/thompson1917-ch16-06> ;
    skos:related <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/thompson1917-ch16-07> ;
    skos:related <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/thompson1917-ch16-16> ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://www.morphosource.org/> ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://doi.org/10.1038/ncomms5855> ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://doi.org/10.1242/jeb.01971> ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.bone.2011.08.020> ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://github.com/fractastical/delphi/blob/ee98025a1960b300fcc06aa2106f51118b60f565/problems/approaches/gemini-4-argon.json> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/problem/trabecular-stress-alignment-wolffs-law> a delphi:Concept, schema:Question ;
    rdfs:label "Do trabeculae align with principal stress, and is that alignment causal?" .

  <https://www.morphosource.org/> dct:title "MorphoSource 3D skeletal micro-CT repository" ;
    dct:description "Search target for comparative and pathological/healed-fracture trabecular bone scans" .
  <https://doi.org/10.1038/ncomms5855> dct:title "Bone remodelling in humans is load-driven but not lazy" ;
    dct:bibliographicCitation "Christen et al. 2014, Bone remodelling in humans is load-driven but not lazy" .
  <https://doi.org/10.1242/jeb.01971> dct:title "Trabecular bone in the bird knee responds with high sensitivity to changes in load orientation" ;
    dct:bibliographicCitation "Pontzer et al. 2006, Trabecular bone in the bird knee responds with high sensitivity to changes in load orientation" .
  <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.bone.2011.08.020> dct:title "A Wolff in sheep's clothing: Trabecular bone adaptation in response to changes in joint loading orientation" ;
    dct:bibliographicCitation "Barak et al. 2011, A Wolff in sheep's clothing: Trabecular bone adaptation in response to changes in joint loading orientation" .
}

